<!-- wp:group {"className":"sb-legal__body"} -->
<div class="wp-block-group sb-legal__body"><!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"who","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="who"><span>01</span> Who we are</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>SEO Booster ("we") runs seobooster.uk and is the controller of the personal data described here. Our registered company details will be added before launch. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@seobooster.uk">hello@seobooster.uk</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"collect","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="collect"><span>02</span> What we collect</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Account and order data:</strong> name, email address, billing address, order history and payment status.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Project details:</strong> website URLs, business name and contact details for listings, keywords, briefs and any files you upload.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Messages:</strong> what you send through our contact and quote forms, or by email.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address and browser information in server logs, kept for security.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"use","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="use"><span>03</span> How and why we use it</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We use your data to take payment and deliver your order (to perform our contract with you), to answer enquiries and keep records (our legitimate interests), to meet tax and accounting rules (legal obligation), and, only if you agree, to send occasional updates.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"share","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="share"><span>04</span> Who we share it with</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We share data only with the services that help us run the site and deliver your order: our payment providers, our hosting provider and our email provider. Where a service requires it, we submit your business details to third-party platforms, for example your name, address and phone number to business directories for a citations order. These are the details you asked us to publish.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"transfers","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="transfers"><span>05</span> International transfers</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some of our providers may process data outside the UK. When they do, we rely on safeguards recognised under UK data protection law, such as adequacy regulations or standard contractual clauses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"retention","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="retention"><span>06</span> How long we keep it</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We keep order and invoice records for six years to meet UK tax rules. Project files and briefs are deleted or archived within 12 months of order completion, unless you ask us to keep them for future work. Contact-form messages that do not lead to an order are deleted after 24 months.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"security","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="security"><span>07</span> How we protect it</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The site uses HTTPS, access to customer data is limited to the people who need it, uploaded files are stored in a protected folder that cannot be opened directly from the web, and we never ask for your passwords.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"rights","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="rights"><span>08</span> Your rights</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to access, correct, delete or receive a copy of your data, and to restrict or object to how we use it. Email <a href="mailto:hello@seobooster.uk">hello@seobooster.uk</a> and we will reply within one month. If you are unhappy with our answer, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at ico.org.uk.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"cookies","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="cookies"><span>09</span> Cookies</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>See our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for the cookies this site uses.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"anchor":"changes","className":"sb-legal__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading sb-legal__h" id="changes"><span>10</span> Changes to this policy</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We will update this page when our practices change and show the date at the top. Significant changes will also be emailed to customers with active orders.</p>
